      "writtenOn": "2020-08-07T23:30:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you very much for your efforts to help me understand all this, very appreciated.\n\n\u003e So it has this MediaPlayer \u0026 MediaRecorder instance as an interface\n  A/ Are you saying that IMS service is not actually using android.media.MediaPlayer as an instance of that object and the existing implementation underneath, but as a general interface that not only has your new OnImsRxNoticeListener interface, but also all the MediaPlayer interface (for instance pause(), setDisplay())?\n  B/ Or do you mean IMS service needs \"some\" interface to get the callback information through any means, and any MediaPlayer instance will be fine to surface it?\n  C/ Or last, your Video-over-LTE player will create a MediaPlayer, and will relay the Rx information to the IMS service?\n\nSorry for the different questions, I want to minimize our back and forth ;-)",
