      "writtenOn": "2020-08-10T08:09:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry for the different questions, I want to minimize our back and forth ;-)\n    ㄴNo worry about this. We already expected there would be lots of exchanging of review \u0026 synchronizing to contribute AOSP master.\n\nA/ The second one. The service actually uses instance of android.media.MediaPlayer and its existing implementation as a general interface as all the other apps does. The service can call all interfaces that include pause() \u0026 setDisplay() also. But it  calls some of the parts it actually needs for ViLTE. Here is list of functions in calling time order.\n\nsetOnImsRxNoticeListener()        \u003c--- What we want to add in now\nsetOnVideoSizeChangedListener()\nsetDataSource()\nsetSurface()\nprepare()\nstart()\nsetRTPBitrate()           \u003c--- Will be added in the next patchset\nstop()\nrelease()\n\nB/ The IMS service needs any means to get feedbacks from MediaPlayer. We found MediaPlayer already have some interfaces to register(setOnBlahBlahListener()) callback and get information through the callback. So we also would like to do same thing for supporting MediaPlayer as an ViLTE player.\nYes, any MediaPlayer instance can do the same thing by adding this interface but it is limited to instances in system level app/service. It is SystemApi and will be limited to app/service who has some previleged permission as you guided.\n\nC/ Our IMS service creates MediaPlayer to use the player as a video player of ViLTE. And the modified MediaPlayer by this code will relay ViLTE Rx(player) information to the IMS service. Absolutely the relay code is ready for native MediaPlayer. Please refer https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/av/+/952489 .\n\n\n   APP             JAVA             JNI              NATIVE  \n\nIMSService ---\u003e RegisterCallback\n\n\nIMSService \u003c--- RegisteredCallback    \u003c-------------    MediaPlayer.notify()\n\n\nThank you for reading!",
